  "formatVersion": 1,
  "name": "Switch drawing (24 ports)",
  "author": "SnmpLens",
  "description": "A 24-port access switch drawn as its front panel: odd ports on the top row, even underneath, uplinks set apart on the right, each box coloured by what that port is actually doing. This is the one example that lists its instances by hand, and that is the feature rather than an oversight — a drawing places its ports, so there is nowhere for a discovered one to go. Edit the numbers, or the drawing, for a switch of another shape. Add a photograph of your own rack in Settings > Presets to draw over it.",
